DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ssoocckkaattmmaarrkk()  returns  a value indicating whether or not the socket re‐
       ferred to by the file descriptor _s_o_c_k_f_d is at the out‐of‐band mark.  If
       the socket is at the mark, then 1 is returned; if the socket is not  at
       the mark, 0 is returned.  This function does not remove the out‐of‐band
       mark.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       A  successful  call  to  ssoocckkaattmmaarrkk() returns 1 if the socket is at the
       out‐of‐band mark, or 0 if it is not.  On error, -1 is returned and  _e_r_‐
       _r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

